        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "A bounded max-heap reduces top-k maintenance work while traversal ordinals preserve earlier-point precedence for equal distances. Capping heap storage at the point count avoids excess heap allocation; rerunning the original scan on a NaN distance preserves its ordering behavior. The controller should evaluate the integrated program's correctness and speed.",
        "id": "79acb1efb2944f8f",
        "ordinal": 2,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "G",
        "source_commits": [
